From bea6a96b0d5b68be9ed9ca879a8b3956eff49717 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:56:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] media: cedrus: add AVS decoding

Add AVS1 (JiZhun) and AVS+ (Guangdian) decoding through the stateless
AVS uAPI. The decoder runs in the H.264 engine slot of the video engine,
like VP8, with VE_MODE set to the H.264 decoder and bit 28 of the
control register selecting AVS. The register layout and the programming
sequence were recovered, for interoperability, from the debug
information and the disassembly of the vendor libawavs.so; no vendor
code is used.

- The engine is started once per picture at the first slice start code
  and parses the slice headers itself, decoding all the slices of the
  picture, of both fields for a field coded picture. Bit 26 of the
  control register makes it remove the pseudo start code bits of the
  slice data. Bitstream initialisation (trigger 7) comes before the
  picture decode trigger (9), as the vendor library does, both with
  start code detection type 1.
- Software provides the sequence header, the picture header with its
  AVS+ tools (AEC, enhanced field B, no forward reference, weighting
  quantisation, as coded), and the picture distances and coding of the
  references. A P picture has two forward references; the engine takes
  the second one in the registers of the backward reference of a B
  picture. A missing reference is replaced by the picture itself.
- Co-located motion vectors (32 bytes per macroblock) are kept per
  capture buffer: I and P pictures write their own, B pictures read
  those of their backward reference. A 48 KiB macroblock information
  buffer per context is placed on a 16 KiB boundary.
- Requests must carry the sequence and picture controls.
- The VE is reset when switching to or from AVS, as for VP9 and AVS2:
  the H.264 slot registers have an AVS specific meaning in this mode.
- Pictures from 16x16 to 1920x1088, 8-bit 4:2:0, decoded to the tiled
  and, where supported, the linear capture formats.

The capability is not enabled for any variant yet.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
